# Attack-path analysis
Final: low | Decider: model_decided | Matrix severity: ignore | Policy adjusted: ignore
## Rationale
Although the code path allows AuthenticatedUsers grants to bypass BlockPublicAcls checks, the default deployment is single-tenant with one configured account/credential. That means authenticated users are already treated as the owner principal, so the bypass does not meaningfully broaden access in typical deployments. The issue remains a policy enforcement gap but with low real-world impact and low likelihood of abuse without multi-principal configurations.
## Likelihood
low - Requires an authenticated client with ACL write permission and a deployment that recognizes multiple authenticated principals; default configuration uses a single account and access key.
## Impact
low - If multiple authenticated principals exist, AuthenticatedUsers grants can expose bucket/object data to any authenticated requester despite BlockPublicAcls. In the default single-tenant configuration, this does not materially expand access beyond the owner account.
## Assumptions
- BlockPublicAcls is enabled on the target bucket/object.
- The deployment allows more than one authenticated principal (multiple credentials or accounts) or treats AuthenticatedUsers exposure as a security concern.
- The service is reachable over the network (ARGMIN_LISTEN_ADDR may be configured to a non-localhost bind).
- Authenticated request capability (valid SigV4 credentials)
- Permission to write bucket/object ACLs
- ACL grants including AuthenticatedUsers
## Path
Attacker(authenticated)
  -> Put*Acl(AuthUsers)
  -> BlockPublicAcls checks AllUsers only
  -> ACL stored
  -> allows_authenticated_users()
  -> Authenticated read access
## Path evidence
- `crates/server-core/src/coordinator.rs:4236-4252` - Authorization allows AuthenticatedUsers, but public ACL detection only checks AllUsers.
- `crates/server-core/src/coordinator.rs:7491-7522` - Bucket ACL updates enforce BlockPublicAcls only when public_read/public_write are set.
- `crates/server-core/src/coordinator.rs:7561-7567` - Object ACL persistence also blocks only on public_read/public_write.
- `crates/s3-types/src/lib.rs:368-488` - AclGrantee includes AuthenticatedUsers and allows_authenticated_users checks for it.
- `crates/argmin-s3/src/main.rs:132-142` - Default runtime loads a single account/credential, limiting multi-tenant impact.
- `crates/argmin-s3/src/config.rs:61-62` - Default listen address is 127.0.0.1:9000; exposure depends on configuration.
## Narrative
ACL grants now include AuthenticatedUsers and authorization explicitly allows authenticated users via allows_authenticated_users(). However, public ACL detection only checks AllUsers, and BlockPublicAcls enforcement during bucket/object ACL updates rejects updates only when public_read/public_write (AllUsers) are set. This allows AuthenticatedUsers grants to be persisted even when BlockPublicAcls is enabled, letting any authenticated requester pass ACL checks. In this repo’s default single-account configuration, all authenticated requests map to the same account, which limits cross-tenant impact and reduces severity.
## Controls
- SigV4 authentication
- ACL authorization checks
- PublicAccessBlock (BlockPublicAcls)
